{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1382352-all-in-on-m20","id":1382352,"title":"All in on M20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-18T11:07:28-07:00","id":1382352,"title":"All in on M20","content":"I am foolish with money. Cooped up at home, I have been hunting down and collecting gaming books. Some Ars Magica stuff, Awakening, old Ascension, and so forth. I already had a few M20 PDFs (Core, BoS, G&amp;M). Then one night, in a fit of impulse, I figured that I might as well cross the line and invest, or I may never get around to it. Been planning on this for a while and kept being a tightwad.<br /> So as I said, I dropped the coin and ordered hard copies of *everything* official M20. I also have PDFs of it all, except Book of the Fallen. But I concluded that, if I am gonna get my gaming group into this, I need hard copy.<br /> And I gotta admit it is a point of pride. The group I play with, the one guy has a massive RPG library. All of the oWoD books except 20th anniversery editions and beyond. Many of the CoD books too, lots of D&amp;D from 2nd and 3rd ed.<br /> So yeah. I did it to earn the awe of my peers. But they look to be beautiful books and Satyros is fun to read. As I said, I have much of the stuff on PDF. I *am* worried abut the core M20 book though. I have read many reports about how the binding is fragile and the spine cracks real quick.<br /> I suppose most of this is justme bragging and feeling boastful. But that last part is a legit concern<br /> <br /> Are the tales of the fragile spine accurate or exaggerated? Or somewhere between?<br /> With the PDF I can print out essential pages and hand outs. But ido not want to print out the whole book! Keep it on hand, but try to use it as little as possible.<br /> Is it just M20 that has the spine issue, because of the size? Does any one have any suggestions on how to reinforce and/or preserve the book?<br /> <br /> And, on a side note, what (if any) outside party material do people recommend? I have the 9 Spheres PDF, the Enlightened Grimoire, and Mystical Armory. They are usefull (though imperfect), and the grimoire is *huge*. Those are PDF only, and it is impractical to print the whole thing on my HP. Does anyone know of a service that would do such a thing at a reasonable price? I looked into Kinkos and that was waaaay to expensive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T15:28:00-07:00","id":1382397,"title":"","content":"For print on demand, maybe Lulu would work? A local copy shop might offer a better deal than Kinko's if you have a bunch to print.<br /> <br /> PDF recommendations:<br /> <br /> If anyone is new to Mage and doesn't get the core concepts, 'Believe in Magick'! would be useful for describing the basic idea of Mage.<br /> <br /> I don't know how interested you are in Marauders. If you want a subtle take where there's a chance for meaning, 'Weighing the Cost' would be useful.<br /> <br /> What are you looking to play in Mage? There are a few additional PDFs but how much they will be of use to you depends on what flavors you like in your Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?keywords=believe+in+magick&amp;x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=&amp;artist=&amp;pfrom=&amp;pto=\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/site-logo-redesignd.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?keywords=believe+in+magick&amp;x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=&amp;artist=&amp;pfrom=&amp;pto=\" target=\"_blank\"> Storytellers Vault - </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?keywords=believe+in+magick&amp;x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=&amp;artist=&amp;pfrom=&amp;pto=\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?keywords=believe+in+magick&amp;x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=&amp;artist=&amp;pfrom=&amp;pto= </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> , wot pdf, nwod pdf, download wod, white wolf, ww, nwod, vtm, mta, mage the ascension, world of darkness </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/257749/Weighing-the-Cost\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/257749.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/257749/Weighing-the-Cost\" target=\"_blank\"> Weighing the Cost - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/257749/Weighing-the-Cost\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/257749/Weighing-the-Cost </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Weighing the Cost - When the teenage daughter of a local Hermetic mage dies in a terrible accident, the mourning father goes to unconscionab </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T15:55:30-07:00","id":1382402,"title":"","content":"I have a kickstarted M20 Core for display and a couple of PoD standards at the table for reference, I've never had any issues with the spines. It may depend on how rough people are with their books, or perhaps there were some bad batches?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T15:57:56-07:00","id":1382403,"title":"","content":"Honestly? For printing Vault books<br /> <br /> *Looks around*<br /> <br /> I just use the work printer and binder.......shhhh.....don't tell anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T00:07:24-07:00","id":1382462,"title":"","content":"I'm the wrong person to talk to about getting things in print; for the past five years or so, I've been moving exclusively to digital, as my living arrangements don't allow me to maintain a physical library of books. So I'll instead focus on \u201cwhat should I get from Storyteller's Vault?\u201d<br /> <br /> In addition to Enlightened Grimoire and Mystic Armory, I'd also recommend Sources of Magick (from the same author). It does a deep dive into Quintessence and related subjects, dealing primarily on Nodes. <br /> <br /> I also recently picked up Ascension's Landscape. There's no crunch in it; but it tackles a wide variety of subjects that the Storyteller should probably consider when deciding what his version of the World of Darkness is like. <br /> <br /> If you ever want to bring Hedge Magic into your game, you'll want to grab two books: the Sorcery Revised supplement for the Revised Edition of Mage, and the Sorcerer's Companion from the Storyteller's Vault. The latter has a whole chapter of advice for using Sorcerer Revised with M20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T00:34:45-07:00","id":1382466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1382352-all-in-on-m20?p=1382462#post1382462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm the wrong person to talk to about getting things in print; for the past five years or so, I've been moving exclusively to digital, as my living arrangements don't allow me to maintain a physical library of books. So I'll instead focus on \u201cwhat should I get from Storyteller's Vault?\u201d<br /> <br /> In addition to Enlightened Grimoire and Mystic Armory, I'd also recommend Sources of Magick (from the same author). It does a deep dive into Quintessence and related subjects, dealing primarily on Nodes.<br /> <br /> I also recently picked up Ascension's Landscape. There's no crunch in it; but it tackles a wide variety of subjects that the Storyteller should probably consider when deciding what his version of the World of Darkness is like.<br /> <br /> If you ever want to bring Hedge Magic into your game, you'll want to grab two books: the Sorcery Revised supplement for the Revised Edition of Mage, and the Sorcerer's Companion from the Storyteller's Vault. The latter has a whole chapter of advice for using Sorcerer Revised with M20.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All this is excellent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T07:38:21-07:00","id":1382521,"title":"","content":"Ascension's Landscape would be quite useful if you're not sure how your Chronicle will work. It makes you think about assumptions of how magic works, how many mages there are, how many sorcerers (linear mages), and so forth.<br /> <br /> I found Sources of Magick less useful, but it does have several theories on Quintessence and Nodes. You can probably snag a bit from the worked examples of Nodes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T16:27:00-07:00","id":1382844,"title":"","content":"The first two books arrived today, and they are beautiful. And huge! The core M20 is two inches thick, and Book of Secrets is one inch.They have glue binding, so I know the spines will eventually crack if I am not careful.<br /> And I am grateful on the tip for Ascension's Landscape. Lots of ideas on how I can tweak a campaign to keep veteran WoD players on their toes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}